Subject: [PATCH] gfx: apply the font visibility lists on every Fedora

The engine's fingerprinting protection hides fonts a person installed from
websites: only the fonts a distribution installs by default (and its language
packs) stay visible. On Linux that needs a list per distribution release. For
Fedora there are lists for 38 and 39 only, and they are never used: the
release number is read from VERSION_ID="…" with quotes, which Ubuntu's
os-release has and Fedora's does not, so every Fedora is "Fedora, unknown
version" and every installed font stays visible. Measured on Fedora 44 with
Firefox 159.0.1: the same 33 of 63 probed families are visible with the
protection off, on, and with privacy.resistFingerprinting.

An unknown Fedora now uses the two newest lists together, as an unknown
Ubuntu already uses the 22.04 and 20.04 lists. They still name what a current
Fedora installs by default (Noto, Liberation, Cantarell, STIX). Fonts outside
them are hidden from web content only while the protection applies: the
browser's own interface, and sites a person exempts from tracking protection,
still see every font.

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: to be reported (Fedora release detection in widget/GfxInfoBase.cpp,
and lists for current releases).
---
--- a/gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp
+++ b/gfx/thebes/gfxFcPlatformFontList.cpp
@@ -2221,8 +2221,18 @@
       return FontVisibility::User;
 
     case Device::Linux_Fedora_any:
-      // We have no font list for this Fedora version
-      return FontVisibility::Unknown;
+      // Nulavio: every Fedora ends up here. There is no list for versions
+      // after 39, and the release number is never read on Fedora, whose
+      // os-release has VERSION_ID without quotes. With no list, all installed
+      // fonts stay visible to websites and the font protection does nothing.
+      // The two newest lists together still name what a current Fedora
+      // installs by default (Noto, Liberation, Cantarell, STIX), as the
+      // Ubuntu case above does for its unknown versions.
+      if (FamilyInList(aName, kBaseFonts_Fedora_39) ||
+          FamilyInList(aName, kBaseFonts_Fedora_38)) {
+        return FontVisibility::Base;
+      }
+      return FontVisibility::User;
 
     case Device::Linux_Fedora_39:
       if (FamilyInList(aName, kBaseFonts_Fedora_39)) {
@@ -2266,7 +2276,11 @@
       break;
 
     case Device::Linux_Fedora_any:
-      // No font list for this Fedora version; see GetVisibilityForFamily().
+      // Nulavio: the two newest lists; see GetVisibilityForFamily().
+      fontLists.AppendElement(std::make_pair(kBaseFonts_Fedora_39,
+                                             std::size(kBaseFonts_Fedora_39)));
+      fontLists.AppendElement(std::make_pair(kBaseFonts_Fedora_38,
+                                             std::size(kBaseFonts_Fedora_38)));
       break;
 
     case Device::Linux_Fedora_39:
